{"text":"MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The UNC bolt kit felt especially useful because its thread sizes match my existing rivet nuts, giving me matching parts for assembly.",
    "Repair tape, quick-bonding glue, screw-mounted magnets and larger wood screws fit my pattern of collecting practical supplies for fastening, mounting and small repairs."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The casters and pegboard hooks require a particular build or compatible mounting setup that my purchases have not established.",
    "Buying epoxy does not mean I currently need a vacuum chamber, and using mounting tape does not establish a need for wide photography tape. The alcohol also needs to suit the surface and cleaning task before I would choose it."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Having workshop tools seemed to be treated as a reason to want almost any workshop accessory, even when it requires a specific project.",
    "My adhesive and resin purchases seemed to suggest broader interest in related products without enough attention to their different uses."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Exact thread sizes and compatibility with supplies I already own matter more to me than a broad connection to DIY work.",
    "I am more ready to choose versatile repair supplies than specialized equipment or bulk accessories whose dimensions, fit or immediate purpose I still need to confirm."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations recognized my fastening and repair interests but sometimes assumed specific projects and compatible setups that my history does not establish."
}"}
